   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## sv3d-turnaround.json\n\nOne image -> a consistent multi-view turnaround (no mesh needed)\n\n**Does:** SV3D_p takes a single image and renders the same object from fixed azimuths. Ships a **21-frame orbit** (18 deg per frame): ~45 s on the 3090 at ~7 GB VRAM, all frames saved, and you take whatever views you need.\n**Why the orbit and not four stops:** measured on `char_knight.png` (E9b) - asking for four independent 90 deg jumps makes the model hallucinate the back badly, because it is a *video* diffusion model and is far better at advancing the camera a little than teleporting it.\nA smooth orbit sampled at the compass points gives a coherent rear view instead of a jumble (compare rows A and C of `3d/evidence/E9b-knight-sv3d-variants.png`). No text prompt is involved and none can be: the node conditions on CLIP *vision* embeds and camera pose only, with an all-zeros negative (see `SV3D_Conditioning.execute`).\n**Picking views:** with 21 frames the increment is 360/20 = 18 deg, so **frame 0 = 0 deg, 5 = 90, 10 = 180, 15 = 270** and frame 20 wraps back to 0 deg. Those four are what `hy3d-multiview-workflow.json` wants for front/left/right/back.\n**The knob that matters:** `batch_size` must equal the last point index + 1. `azimuth_points_string` `0:(0.0), 9:(180.0), 20:(360.0)` is a full orbit; put more points in for finer sampling. Elevation stays 0 for a level turnaround. `VideoLinearCFGGuidance` is required (SV3D is an image-to-video model); 25 steps / cfg 2.5 is fine - 40/3.5 changed nothing much.\n**Licence:** the SV3D weights are Stability **non-commercial** (commercial use needs a Stability Membership), so anything shipped from this flow inherits that - same posture as Kontext and 4x-UltraSharp in the 2D scenario. The weights live in `models/checkpoints/sv3d_p.safetensors` and are gated on Hugging Face (`stabilityai/sv3d`).\n**See:** `3d/EXPERIMENTS.md` E9/E9b, `3d/README.md`.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S12** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E9** in the scenario's `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "properties": {},
   "order": 0
  }
